# What a trimmed vip build keeps loadable even though the board does not load it today.
# Applied by scripts/build/vip-ubuntu-rt.sh after `make localmodconfig` (the trim): each
# line is a deliberate exception, with a reason.
#
# snd-usb-audio — the bench and soak history was built on USB interfaces (the SSL 2+ on piv),
# and a future measurement on vip may use one. Without this module such a box would need a
# kernel rebuild before it could even try. Its media-controller sub-option and the usbmidi
# library ride along as dependencies; the fragment only sets the one module symbol.
CONFIG_SND_USB_AUDIO=m
# cdc_acm — the Pico's USB console. The Pico 2 W sits on vip's USB on the bench (2e8a:0009,
# "Raspberry Pi Pico", three interfaces: CDC comm, CDC data, vendor), and its firmware puts the
# debug console on USB CDC while the pedal's protocol link stays on the header UART
# (pedal.project firmware/CMakeLists.txt, docs/uart-protocol.md). This is the one keep-list
# entry that could never survive the trim on its own: while the module is absent nothing binds
# the Pico, so cdc_acm can never appear in the board's /proc/modules — a self-fulfilling
# absence, the same shape as the inet_diag note below.
CONFIG_USB_ACM=m
# inet_diag, tcp_diag, mptcp_diag — loaded on demand by ss and friends, and ss is literally
# inside vip-boot-validate. Whether the trim keeps them therefore depends on what happened to
# be loaded when /proc/modules was fetched: the first trimmed build had all three, and a
# rebuild later the same day (nothing using ss at fetch time) dropped them. Keep them so the
# diagnostics — and the validate hook — never depend on the fetch-day load state.
CONFIG_INET_DIAG=m
CONFIG_INET_TCP_DIAG=m
CONFIG_INET_MPTCP_DIAG=m
#
# Note on ac97_bus and snd_compress: the board loads both, but only as dependency edges out
# of snd-soc-core (its selectors, SND_SOC_AC97_BUS and SND_SOC_COMPRESS, were on because of
# codec drivers the trim removes). In the trimmed kernel snd-soc-core has no ac97/compress
# references at all (verified: zero undefined symbols), so the modules would never load and
# are recorded as deliberate removals in the build script's TRIMMED_OK, not kept here.
